    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u20.d01.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "Verb + -ing (gerund)",
        "ru": "Глагол + -ing (герундий)"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "Some verbs are followed by the -ing form (the gerund). Common ones: enjoy, mind, avoid, finish, keep, practise, suggest, imagine. Learn these as a group.",
        "ru": "После некоторых глаголов идёт форма на -ing (герундий). Частые: enjoy, mind, avoid, finish, keep, practise, suggest, imagine. Запоминай их группой."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "enjoy / like + -ing",
            "ru": "enjoy / like + -ing"
          },
          "formula": "enjoy/mind/avoid + verb-ing",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "I enjoy cooking.",
              "ru": "Я люблю готовить."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "finish / keep + -ing",
            "ru": "finish / keep + -ing"
          },
          "formula": "finish/keep/practise + verb-ing",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "She kept talking for an hour.",
              "ru": "Она говорила без остановки целый час."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "suggest / imagine + -ing",
            "ru": "suggest / imagine + -ing"
          },
          "formula": "suggest/imagine + verb-ing",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "He suggested taking a break.",
              "ru": "Он предложил сделать перерыв."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "gerund-infinitive"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "After these verbs use -ing, not \"to\": \"I enjoy cooking\", not \"I enjoy to cook\".",
          "ru": "После этих глаголов — -ing, а не «to»: «I enjoy cooking», а не «I enjoy to cook»."
        },
        {
          "en": "\"suggest\" takes -ing, not \"to\": \"suggested going\", not \"suggested to go\".",
          "ru": "«suggest» с -ing, не «to»: «suggested going», а не «suggested to go»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u20.d01.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "A free afternoon",
        "ru": "Свободный день"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u20.d01.reading.b1",
          "en": "On Sundays, Leo enjoys doing nothing. He avoids checking his email and keeps his phone in a drawer. \"I don't mind spending the whole day at home,\" he says. \"I like reading, cooking, and watching old films.\"",
          "ru": "По воскресеньям Лео любит ничего не делать. Он избегает проверять почту и держит телефон в ящике. «Я не против провести весь день дома, — говорит он. — Люблю читать, готовить и смотреть старые фильмы».",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u20.d01.reading.b1.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u20.d01.reading.b2",
          "en": "This Sunday, his friend suggested going for a walk. \"Good idea,\" said Leo, \"but first I want to finish making lunch.\" They spent the afternoon walking in the park and imagining what they would do on holiday.",
          "ru": "В это воскресенье друг предложил пойти прогуляться. «Хорошая идея, — сказал Лео, — но сначала я хочу доготовить обед». Они провели день, гуляя в парке и представляя, что будут делать в отпуске.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u20.d01.reading.b2.wav",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "glossary": [
        {
          "word": "drawer",
